  "response": "```python\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\n\ndef business_days(date1, date2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Count business days (Monday-Friday) between two dates.\n    Both dates are excluded from the count.\n\n    Parameters:\n        date1 (str): First date in 'YYYY-MM-DD' format\n        date2 (str): Second date in 'YYYY-MM-DD' format\n\n    Returns:\n        int: Number of business days strictly between the two dates\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        d1 = datetime.strptime(date1, '%Y-%m-%d')\n        d2 = datetime.strptime(date2, '%Y-%m-%d')\n    except ValueError as e:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid date format. Expected YYYY-MM-DD: {e}\")\n\n    if d1 == d2:\n        return 0\n\n    start, end = (d1, d2) if d1 < d2 else (d2, d1)\n\n    count = 0\n    current_date = start + timedelta(days=1)\n\n    while current_date < end:\n        if current_date.weekday() < 5:  # Monday is 0, Friday is 4\n            count += 1\n        current_date += timedelta(days=1)\n\n    return count\n```\n\n**Example:**\n```python\nprint(business_days(\"2024-01-01\", \"2024-01-08\"))  # Output: 4\n# Between Jan 1 (Mon) and Jan 8 (Mon): Jan 2–5 are weekdays (4 days); Jan 6–7 are weekend\n\nprint(business_days(\"2024-01-05\", \"2024-01-10\"))  # Output: 2\n# Jan 5 (Fri), Jan 6–7 (weekend), Jan 8 (Mon), Jan 9 (Tue) = 2 business days\n```",
